{
  "source": "course-assets/layers/layers.mp4",
  "duration": 203.3706875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.6,
      "text": "Have you ever read a passage in English class that only made sense after a few reads?"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.26,
      "end": 5.86,
      "text": "Try the sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.04,
      "end": 9.08,
      "text": "The horse raced past the barn fell."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.08,
      "end": 11.74,
      "text": "On the first read, it doesn't make sense."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.44,
      "end": 13.84,
      "text": "It feels like someone forgot a word."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.44,
      "end": 17.16,
      "text": "You reach fell, and the sentence just seems to stop short."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.02,
      "end": 18.78,
      "text": "So you read it again."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.54,
      "end": 20.82,
      "text": "Wait, did a barn fall?"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.28,
      "end": 23.34,
      "text": "Or did the horse race past the barn afterward?"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.06,
      "end": 28.48,
      "text": "You test each possibility against the words to see if fell goes with the barn or with"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.48,
      "end": 28.8,
      "text": "the horse."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.52,
      "end": 30.66,
      "text": "Finally, the meaning clicks."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.28,
      "end": 33.04,
      "text": "Someone raced a horse past a barn."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.66,
      "end": 34.48,
      "text": "Then the horse fell."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.08,
      "end": 38.08,
      "text": "Race describes the horse, and fell is what the horse did."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.62,
      "end": 41.78,
      "text": "Working the sentence out depends entirely on these repeated passes."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.56,
      "end": 44.54,
      "text": "Each read updates the meaning until it clicks."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.64,
      "end": 46.88,
      "text": "AI does something similar."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.52,
      "end": 49.28,
      "text": "It builds meaning through repeated updates."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.92,
      "end": 51.92,
      "text": "AI doesn't read your message the way you do."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.3,
      "end": 54.5,
      "text": "It processes your text through a series of layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.5,
      "end": 60.84,
      "text": "Within each layer, steps called attention and transformation work together to update"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.84,
      "end": 64.38,
      "text": "the numbers, helping the system work out what your words mean together."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.24,
      "end": 67.86,
      "text": "The whole stack of layers is called a neural network."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.6,
      "end": 72.06,
      "text": "Numbers go in on one side, and final numbers come out the other."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.7,
      "end": 78.42,
      "text": "In between stands a long line of layers, one after another, each containing attention and"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.42,
      "end": 78.94,
      "text": "transformation."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.77,
      "end": 84.56,
      "text": "Each row of data passing through contains many numbers, but we are going to focus on"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.56,
      "end": 85.9,
      "text": "just two to track the change."
    },
    {
      "start": 86.66,
      "end": 90.52,
      "text": "We start with a pair at .42 and negative 1.15."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.16,
      "end": 97.34,
      "text": "As they pass through the layers, the values shift at every single step, finishing at .19"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.34,
      "end": 99.18,
      "text": "and negative 1.12."
    },
    {
      "start": 99.88,
      "end": 102.56,
      "text": "The numbers that come out are not the numbers that went in."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.12,
      "end": 106.38,
      "text": "Attention and transformation update the numbers at each layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.96,
      "end": 112.12,
      "text": "Now let's follow a single word, it, to see how its numbers change in a real sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.62,
      "end": 116.38,
      "text": "The cat sat on the mat during the May rainstorm because it was tired."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.94,
      "end": 119.7,
      "text": "At the start, the word it could refer to different things."
    },
    {
      "start": 120.44,
      "end": 125.26,
      "text": "The starting numbers .12 and negative .34 don't tell us which one."
    },
    {
      "start": 126.04,
      "end": 130.96,
      "text": "By layer one, the numbers update, beginning to capture a connection between it and cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.54,
      "end": 134.26,
      "text": "Moving into layer two, the numbers update again."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.81,
      "end": 138.22,
      "text": "Now they carry even more specific information about that connection."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.08,
      "end": 140.0,
      "text": "This process repeats."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.7,
      "end": 142.04,
      "text": "It doesn't stop at layer two."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.6,
      "end": 147.2,
      "text": "The numbers continue passing through more layers, each building directly on the previous"
    },
    {
      "start": 147.2,
      "end": 148.02,
      "text": "layer's numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 148.74,
      "end": 153.22,
      "text": "By the result stage, the two numbers finish at .41 and .06."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.9,
      "end": 156.2,
      "text": "AI works out that it refers to cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 156.98,
      "end": 162.3,
      "text": "While AI companies don't always share exactly how many layers their models use, published designs"
    },
    {
      "start": 162.3,
      "end": 166.22,
      "text": "show architectures built with dozens and sometimes more than a hundred layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 167.14,
      "end": 173.5,
      "text": "The horse sentence took a few reeds to untangle, sarcasm, story twists, and complicated reasoning"
    },
    {
      "start": 173.5,
      "end": 174.94,
      "text": "can take even more work."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.64,
      "end": 179.64,
      "text": "AI's layers give it more steps to work through those relationships and build meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 180.36,
      "end": 184.6,
      "text": "If more layers give the system better reasoning, why not just keep adding them infinitely?"
    },
    {
      "start": 185.44,
      "end": 189.36,
      "text": "Because adding layers demands massive amounts of computing power and time."
    },
    {
      "start": 189.66,
      "end": 192.06,
      "text": "The extra benefit has to be worth the cost."
    },
    {
      "start": 192.9,
      "end": 194.88,
      "text": "Meaning builds up layer by layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 195.68,
      "end": 197.16,
      "text": "Attention and transformation."
    },
    {
      "start": 198.08,
      "end": 198.84,
      "text": "Dozens of times."
    }
  ],
